{
 "what": "Encode of 100000 CTAP2 getAssertion responses into one padded span: schema with fixed fields, schema with variable fields, generic with variable fields. ns per record. Arm old: main 42ff269. Arm new: the same header with a check in internal::head_write that writes exactly when fewer than 9 bytes remain to the end of the buffer.",
 "why": "The check is needed for an exact writer into MDB_RESERVE. The owner asked what it costs on the padded path.",
 "how": "Google Benchmark, one binary per arm, each built twice (a, b). 5 rounds alternating old_a new_a old_b new_b, each with --benchmark_repetitions=5 --benchmark_enable_random_interleaving=true.",
 "finding": "The check costs about 15 percent in generic and 7 percent in schema with variable fields, and nothing in schema with fixed fields, which writes no head through head_write. Noise between a and b is under 0.5 ns.",
